{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/461783-castigations-and-vestments","id":461783,"title":"Castigations and Vestments","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-29T20:01:39-07:00","id":461783,"title":"Castigations and Vestments","content":"Does anyone see any issues regarding using the Family Vestment Castigation to pick up Vestments from <i>Inferno</i>? I was thinking that maybe you could use your Castigation rating instead of your rating in individual Sins.<br /> <br /> I was thinking that 1-dot or 2-dot Vestments would be the most appropriate; 2-dot Vestments would replace their costs with those of Family Vestment.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T00:50:00-07:00","id":461983,"title":"","content":"Well, three things.<br /> <br /> First of all, using castigation as vice rating? They'd be more powerful than the demon possessed, which doesn't seem right.<br /> <br /> Second of all, I think some of the vestments are a bit much as hunter powers, unless using the dread power rules.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, it doesn't match the fluff- castigation is proprietary because only the lucifuge are taught how to wield demonic power that way,which is obviously isn't the case with vestments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T01:21:16-07:00","id":462020,"title":"","content":"I dont see a reason why not. To adress Swords points:<br /> <br /> The Lucifuge are scions of Hell while the Possessed merely draw on the fragmentary power the Demon allows them to. The Lucifuge have full acess to that power themselves. Its fine if they have a few more dice than the Possessed.<br /> True, some of the powers are a bit much, but specifically for a Lucifuge, I dont think thats such a big issue. If you play up the fact that this is demonic power, and useing it too much and too often will further Hells agenda (And perhaps turn you more demonic and insane?) then it'll effectively become a sort of Faustian Bargain, which is in line with the Lucifuge.<br /> It can easily be made to fit fluff-wise. Its just a Castigation that mimics the power of a Vestment. It isn't actually that Vestment, but it sure seems like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T04:18:45-07:00","id":462086,"title":"","content":"So what stops the demons from reverse engineering castigation rituals, if it's so easy to reverse engineer demonic power? <br /> <br /> As for power levels, lucifuge are humans with tricks, the possessed are a template, humans with tricks don't outrank templates, that's kind of the point of templates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T05:01:54-07:00","id":462111,"title":"","content":"The problem with the Lucifuge is that they have a weird place in the WoD. Mechanically, they are hunters- that is, humans with tricks. On the other, their life span increase with their status, they have inborn powers, you can't just &quot;join&quot; them and learn their tricks, they have a transmutative experience called the Becoming and you have examples of other Children of 7th Generation where their mechanics are describe as including Infernal Aspects/ Dread Powers, Vestments and even Numina and stranger powers. The Lucifuge are in the big World of Darkness- so calling them &quot;Humans with Tricks&quot; kinds miss their point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T06:13:28-07:00","id":462157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/461783-castigations-and-vestments?p=462086#post462086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what stops the demons from reverse engineering castigation rituals, if it's so easy to reverse engineer demonic power?<br /> <br /> As for power levels, lucifuge are humans with tricks, the possessed are a template, humans with tricks don't outrank templates, that's kind of the point of templates.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Lostlight said, they are certainly not just &quot;humans with tricks&quot;, atleast from a fluff perpective. You are correct though, that from a mechanical perspective, they are just that. But I were never a fan of modeling fluff after systems, and was always a big fan of modding systems to fit with the fluff.<br /> As I said, a Lucifuge is a scion of hell. Within their soul lies the burning power of the Inferno itself. While an unfettered demon might be able to harness greater powers in the short time it can exist free of its human host - before being dragged back to Hell - a human possessed by a Demon simply cannot harness the full scale of the demonic power, without suffering immense Burnout. The demoncally possessed human is simply an aspirant of Hells power. The Lucifuge is the real deal.<br /> That said, none of the Castigation Rituals are powerful enough, that I dont see why a Possessed character shouldn't be able to pick them as a Vestment, at Storyteller approval. That is, if they can find a Vice to flavor them through.<br /> Thats the defineing characteristic between Castigations and Vestments, the way I see it. Vestments are the literal power of Hell as filtered through the Demons own understanding of that power. Since the Demon is an inherently Vice-driven thing, those powers must also be flavored through the Demons understanding, and all it understands is Vice.<br /> The Lucifuge on the other hand, has learned a way to utilize Hells power to which they have acess, without the corruptive influence of Vice seeping into them. Thats the Castigations. Since the evil, selfish cruelty has been somehow filtered out, they dont nessesarily need to be associated with a Vice.<br /> <br /> I've given this some decent amount of thought, and have more or less introduced the Lucifuge/Le Enfants Diabolic as a minor template for a handful of NPC's in one of my chronicles, so this is a subject I am rather interested in discussing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T10:09:06-07:00","id":462388,"title":"","content":"The Possessed are only a template because we didn't have unified Ephemeral Being rules; otherwise, they'd probably be Claimed. If I were to bring the Lucifuge to full &quot;minor template&quot; status, they would probably end up eating the Possessed (as in, the Possessed would be a subset).<br /> <br /> Also, looking over some of the benefits, I think using [Castigation] in place of the normal Sin rating is a bit too much; I'd probably revise that initial guesstimate to [(Castigation+1)/2]. Heck, they're weaker than Possessed in some key areas because they lack an Infernal Willpower pool.<br /> <hr /><br /> As for thematics, Le Enfants Diabolic aren't possessed by demons, and they aren't learning demonic powers as rituals... the rituals they learn are <i>control mechanisms</i>. Because they would develop their powers naturally even if they didn't go through the Becoming (and would probably be at Integrity 1 <i>real</i> quick). Because, on a certain level? They <i>are</i> demons.<br /> <br /> They've got that truth running through their veins; their tongues are forked with the authority of Hell and their eyes brim with the cold certainty of a sinner's punishment. Heck, a Lucifuge is actually <i>technically</i> more &quot;Hell Authority&quot; than a Possessed - compare Mandate of Hell to Chain of Command.<br /> <br /> They aren't &quot;reverse engineering&quot;, so much as they are calling on what is rightfully theirs.<br /> <br /> (And if I were running a Possessed game, I'd be pretty cool with letting players take Castigations as Vestments. Of course, since this is the <i>Inferno</i> forum... oh, wait, it isn't. This is the <i>Hunter</i> forum, and therefore Hunters get the attention.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T19:58:06-07:00","id":464200,"title":"","content":"And since OP doesn't have the funds to send canon ninja to arrange accidents, you can do what you like. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That doesn't change the fact that lucifuge aren't a template, that castigation is a merit, and that merits don't trump supernatural powers in the world of darkness.<br /> <br /> Mandate of Hell is inferior to Lord of Demons, it summons a demon, it works for a full scene, and the demon has no resistance roll. Which is as it should be, one is a full fledged supernatural power, the other is a merit. As for Mandate of Hell's superiority over Chain of Command? Extremely debateable. Automatic success against every demon of rank 1 or 2, versus a roll against a demon's resistance that needs an extended roll for commands that take any time? You are aware that at rank 3 a demon's resistance can be 9, so a lucifuge commanding a demon of rank 3 is going to be extremely short lived to nonexistent, right? Plus a lucifuge confronted by ten rank 2 demons is screwed, a demon possessed with chain of command has a rock band and some roadies, without a single roll, right? <br /> <br /> Also, if the writers wanted demonic power to all be the same, they wouldn't have expressly written otherwise. Castigation is different from dread powers which is different from enfant demonic aspects.<br /> <br /> There are rules for lucifuge gaining full fledged dread powers though, they cost 6 points per level, so giving the lucifuge access to a full fledged demonic power at merit costs is not appropriate to hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 03-31-2015, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T21:14:10-07:00","id":464249,"title":"","content":"Umm... No. You just described <i>neither</i> of Mandate of Hell or Lord of Demons. You're thinking of Calling Forth the Pit.<br /> <br /> Lord of Demons forces demons with a Rank of 2 or less to obey your commands.<br /> <br /> Mandate of Hell is a Presence + Composure vs. Resistance Instant Action that forces a demon of <i>any Rank</i> to obey <i>any</i> command for a turn, which can also be used as an Extended Action to give a demon a complex command (the example given is &quot;Go to the corner of 7th and Maple, kill the man you find there, and afterwards, return to Hell and do not return&quot;.) <s>Even with the &quot;basic&quot; version, the Lucifuge could give <i>Satan himself</i> the order to disembowel himself, and they have <i>at least</i> a 1 in ten chance of it working.</s> I misread it as a Resisted action rather than a Contested. Oops. Still, it's really good, especially considering stuff like Risking Willpower.<br /> <br /> One of those is <i>considerably</i> more powerful than the other. And it belongs to the Lucifuge.<br /> <br /> The thing you seem to be forgetting is that both Hunters <i>and</i> the Possessed are templates; if you call Hunters &quot;humans with tricks&quot;, then I can, <i>with equal validity</i>, call the Possessed &quot;humans with tricks&quot;. <hr /><br /> As for Dread Powers... I forgot about that; I think the adjusted cost as-per Mortal Remains is 2xp per dot, but that might just be for monsters. <hr /><br /> Anyway, this thread specifically asks about <i>issues</i> that might arise were I to allow equivalents to be used as Family Vestments. Your responses are... kinda not <i>helpful</i>. Except for the bit about Dread Powers (which aren't really comparable to Vestments.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 04-01-2015, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}